      "reasons": [
        "The packet text specifically describes *distortion-product* otoacoustic emissions (responses to two tones of a given frequency and sound pressure level). The provided definition presents otoacoustic emissions as a general method without limiting it to distortion-product, which is not directly supported by the packet’s wording.",
        "Because the packet’s support is for distortion-product otoacoustic emissions, the definition’s broader phrasing (“a noninvasive test… before neural processing”) for *otoacoustic emissions* in general is an unsupported generalization beyond what the packet explicitly states."
